  with "fatal error: 'WKAPICastWin.h' file not found" at WKAPICast.h:444
  as soon as the round-25 PCH fixes let the unified sources compile.
  Skip the include when BUILDING_GTK__ is defined: OptionsGTK.cmake
  defines it globally for every GTK-port target, the GTK cast table
  (WKAPICastGtk.h, included just above) already maps WKViewRef to
  WebKitWebViewBase, and the Win header's sole content -
  WK_ADD_API_MAPPING(WKViewRef, WebView) for the CA port's WebView
  class - has no GTK-port consumer; including both would conflict, as
  both headers define toAPI<>/toImpl<> specializations for WKViewRef.
  Ports that do not define BUILDING_GTK__ keep upstream behavior.

  Update 27 (fixing the round-27 CLANG64 WebKit IPC unified-source
  failures, first hit at UnifiedSource-Platform-2/4.cpp [8192/8564]):
  the previous rounds' Windows IPC plumbing was flavor-inconsistent -
  Attachment.h kept the upstream OS(WINDOWS) HANDLE-based struct while
  the GTK port's SourcesGTK.txt manifest compiles the unix-flavored
  IPC sources (glib/ConnectionGLib.cpp, unix/ArgumentCodersUnix.cpp,
  unix/IPCSemaphoreUnix.cpp, unix/IPCUtilitiesUnix.cpp) against
  USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)-selected flavors of Connection.h
